      "result": "\n\nWritten to `submission/main.c`. Summary of how it meets each requirement:\n\n1. **Devicetree lookup** — `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(dma0))` with a NULL check.\n2. **Readiness check** — `device_is_ready()` before any DMA API call.\n3. **Buffers** — 64-byte aligned (32-byte) `src_buf`/`dst_buf`; source filled with pattern `1..64`, destination zeroed via `memset`.\n4. **Channel config** — `struct dma_config` with `DMA_DIRECTION_MEMORY_TO_MEMORY`, `DMA_MODE_M2M`, op size 4, full buffer size, `DMA_SLOT_ANY`, passed to `dma_config()`.\n5. **Callback** — `dma_callback_set()` with a completion callback that records driver-reported errors and signals a semaphore.\n6. **Wait** — `k_sem_take(&dma_sem, K_SECONDS(5))`; on timeout it stops the channel and returns.\n7. **Verification** — `memcmp(dst_buf, src_buf, 64)`.\n8. **Result print** — success/failure message via `printk`.\n9. **Error handling** — each step (device, config, callback set, start, timeout, DMA status error, verification mismatch) has its own diagnostic message and error return.\n\nThe app then idles in a sleep loop so the result stays observable on the console. Note it assumes the `dma0` label exists in the devicetree (a short example overlay is in the file header comment), since the app itself is a single `main.c` per the task spec.",
